*  KW-5b witness: the keyword block's oracle-true INITIAL VALUES must be live
*  before statement one, for a program that never mentions a keyword at all.
*  &TRIM's oracle default is 1 (FINDING s146 §3 -- the oracle disagrees with
*  its own manual p.191 here, and the oracle wins), so a line read from a file
*  arrives with its trailing blanks and tabs already stripped.
*  SCRIP s161: seeding ran LAZILY at the first keyword touch, so THIS program
*  -- which touches none -- ran on the C initializers and read back the
*  untrimmed line, while the very same program with one '&ANCHOR' read in
*  front of it read back the trimmed one.  The answer depended on access
*  order.  Input (kw_trim_lazy_seed.dat): "hello   " then "world<TAB>".
	L = INPUT
	OUTPUT = '[' L ']'
	OUTPUT = 'size=' SIZE(L)
	M = INPUT
	OUTPUT = '[' M ']'
	OUTPUT = 'size=' SIZE(M)
END
